Pi-hole core scripts as a FenrirOS package (written for FenrirOS).

Upstream installs the core by cloning its git repository to /etc/.pihole and
the `pihole` command to /usr/local/bin, and updates itself from git. Here the
package owns the files:
- the read-only copy of the core tree is /usr/share/pihole/core (was
  /etc/.pihole), the command /usr/bin/pihole (was /usr/local/bin);
- `pihole -up`, `repair`, `uninstall` and `checkout` say that apk manages
  Pi-hole (the same path upstream's Docker image takes) instead of running
  git or the installer;
- updatecheck.sh reads each component's version and commit from a
  .fenrir-version file the package writes, instead of asking git.
